name><surname>Moe</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Honorat</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Leon</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Eisenberg</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Epidemiologic patterns of published norovirus outbreak reports, 1981&#x02013;2006.</article-title><source>Program and Abstracts of Third International Calicivirus Conference</source><fpage>39</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005058-Hedlund1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hedlund</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Hjertqvist</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lysen</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Norovirus genogroup I dominates in Swedish Waterborne Outbreaks.</article-title><source>Program and Abstracts of Third International Calicivirus Conference</source><fpage>38</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005058-Prasad1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Prasad</surname><given-names>BV</given-names></name><name><surname>Hardy</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Dokland</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Bella</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Rossmann</surname><given-names>MG</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>X-ray crystallographic structure of the Norwalk virus capsid.</article-title><source>Science</source><volume>286</volume><fpage>287</fpage><lpage>290</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10514371</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005058-Bu1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-ty